Title: Link crypt32.lib into libnode on Windows
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

src/crypto/crypto_context.cc reads the Windows certificate store under
#ifdef _WIN32 -- CertOpenStore, CertEnumCertificatesInStore,
CertGetEnhancedKeyUsage, CertCloseStore -- but libnode's GN target only
declares psapi.lib. Node's own GYP build picks crypt32.lib up transitively from
deps/openssl (deps/openssl/unofficial.gni declares it), which Electron does not
build: node_openssl_path points at //third_party/boringssl, and BoringSSL's GN
target does not link crypt32.

electron.exe links anyway, because //net and //crypto each add crypt32.lib and
it ends up on the link line. node_mksnapshot.exe links libnode with neither, so
a native Windows build fails with:

  lld-link: error: undefined symbol: __declspec(dllimport) CertOpenStore
  >>> referenced by third_party/electron_node/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc

A Linux-hosted cross build does not hit this: v8_snapshot_toolchain is the host
toolchain there, so node_mksnapshot is built as a host (Linux) binary.

diff --git a/unofficial.gni b/unofficial.gni
index 28cf0d2d..bc75b396 100644
--- a/unofficial.gni
+++ b/unofficial.gni
@@ -226,7 +226,19 @@ template("node_gn_build") {
     ] + gypi_values.node_sources
 
     if (is_win) {
-      libs = [ "psapi.lib" ]
+      libs = [
+        "psapi.lib",
+
+        # src/crypto/crypto_context.cc reads the Windows certificate store
+        # (CertOpenStore, CertEnumCertificatesInStore, CertGetEnhancedKeyUsage,
+        # CertCloseStore) under #ifdef _WIN32. Node's own build gets this
+        # transitively from deps/openssl, but Electron unbundles OpenSSL to
+        # //third_party/boringssl, which does not link it. electron.exe happens
+        # to resolve these anyway because //net and //crypto both add
+        # crypt32.lib, but node_mksnapshot.exe links libnode without either and
+        # fails with "undefined symbol: CertOpenStore" and friends.
+        "crypt32.lib",
+      ]
     }
     if (is_mac) {
       frameworks = [
